        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                "word": "opperwezen",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "98722eb9-a825-4155-a5c8-fec81c702b9d",
                        "entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "opperwezens"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                        "entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een hypothetisch bovennatuurlijke entiteit die door gelovigen als machtig, bovenmenselijk wezen wordt aanbeden en verantwoordelijk wordt geacht voor bepaalde aspecten van de werkelijkheid, dan wel voor de werkelijkheid als geheel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd7319d2-baea-4f69-8049-0d00c83aff1f",
                                "sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                                "text": "\"Nee hoor, ik ben geen maagd omdat een of ander opperwezen andere plannen met mij heeft, ik bewaar mezelf gewoon voor mezelf. Ik bewaar mezelf dus ook niet voor iemand anders. Zo romantisch ben ik niet. Ik bewaar mezelf helemaal voor mezelf.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f19f9ab-9dcb-4402-805f-0ad0b88a036d",
                                "sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                                "text": "\"En dat is seks,\"zeg ik dan. \"Het is naar de sterren vliegen zonder hulp van de wetenschap of een opperwezen.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9191d7cf-4f6b-4fc3-9509-c461e43c51fa",
                                "sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                                "text": "Van huis uit was Wessels orthodox gereformeerd, maar gaandeweg nam hij afstand. „Ik leef christelijk, maar ga niet naar de kerk”, zei hij in het interview met Quote. En ook: „Ik mijd deze gesprekken liever. Ik geloof wel dat er een Opperwezen is, maar het is lastig te bevatten. Ik kan alles begrijpen in deze wereld, maar op godsdienst krijg ik geen grip.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4fe9ad2f-4f05-420c-ad25-36c19a559b20",
                        "source_entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                        "target_lang_word": "Lord of Heaven",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a499be5b-d561-4668-8618-9c7f3833e3f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                        "target_lang_word": "Creator",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Creator",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cf8e0b7-801c-3391-94d0-b1b60675af7b",
                                        "entry_id": "f7c2e136-7388-3c88-8aad-fa2f3a0e27b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A god who created the Universe; God."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82924f83-d402-4f5a-9ce2-ec1067c30c56",
                                                "sense_id": "9cf8e0b7-801c-3391-94d0-b1b60675af7b",
                                                "text": "Who changed the trueth of God into a lye, and worshipped and serued the creature more then the Creatour, who is blessed for euer. Amen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a3ec3e3-2865-415d-8bad-2217e8457267",
                                                "sense_id": "9cf8e0b7-801c-3391-94d0-b1b60675af7b",
                                                "text": "\"Whether a child is born in the urban sprawl of Detroit or the windswept plains of Nebraska, they look up at the same night sky, they fill their heart with the same dreams, and they are infused with the breath of life by the same almighty Creator.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28bbc4de-17ef-4127-9d0f-aea3dbb211e7",
                                                "sense_id": "9cf8e0b7-801c-3391-94d0-b1b60675af7b",
                                                "text": "“The notion that rights don’t come from laws and don’t come from the government, but come from the Creator — that’s what the Iranian government believes,” he said. “It’s a theocratic regime that bases its rule on Shia (sic) law and targets Sunnis, Bahá’ís, Jews, Christians, and other religious minorities. They do it because they believe that they understand what natural rights are from their Creator. So, the statement that our rights do not come from our laws or our governments is extremely troubling.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6143c018-9ed3-4eb9-870a-4e407350be01",
                        "source_entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                        "target_lang_word": "Heavenly Father",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Heavenly Father",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "000b639b-f1f3-3604-b8c0-0bd732d10873",
                                        "entry_id": "c0289680-0735-34d7-8e6b-16a322dd38fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Jewish or Christian God; among Trinitarians, especially God the Father."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ee0d9ba-aeaa-4589-91d2-499a40dda320",
                                                "sense_id": "000b639b-f1f3-3604-b8c0-0bd732d10873",
                                                "text": "For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "19ed0de1-b6c7-4d88-95ef-14183b19ff72",
                        "source_entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                        "target_lang_word": "Omnipotence",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cdf6f08a-9466-4047-bca6-556189de8849",
                        "source_entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                        "target_lang_word": "God",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "God",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                        "entry_id": "c263d298-916a-3a90-b069-45bbe6034df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The first deity of various theistic religions, and the only deity in monotheism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f2d027f-66b3-4890-9502-8d0614d7c538",
                                                "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                                "text": "Dawn believes in God, but Willow believes in multiple gods and goddesses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "604e45ca-4d00-4bf8-b8a9-df20957859a6",
                                                "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                                "text": "Hee that loueth not, knoweth not God: for God is loue"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cd2b9df-847a-464a-8337-e937b3e29b9a",
                                                "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                                "text": "God is loue, and hee that dwelleth in loue, dwelleth in God, and God in him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "668f24ed-b433-4241-b08b-eb9e807278af",
                                                "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                                "text": "...God, the All-gracious, the All-good, the All-bountiful, the All-mighty, the All-merciful God..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2126fbe-869e-496b-b3cd-d4748b20287c",
                                                "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                                "text": "The Muéddin: God is great, there is no God but God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a22521bc-cc4b-4a05-8360-ca7a8d7ae36b",
                                                "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                                "text": "This is a sad time for all people. We have suffered a loss that cannot be weighed. For me, it is a deep personal tragedy. I know that the world shares the sorrow that Mrs. Kennedy and her family bear. I will do my best. That is all I can do. I ask for your help — and God's."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3bd396c-4972-4ca9-bbbd-1a39de914afa",
                                                "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                                "text": "He (n.b.: a Muslim) has told me that he will not allow one person’s actions to stop him from praying to his God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fafd1e0-bfd9-43a0-aeaf-70a5cd84c63f",
                                                "sense_id": "c407551a-0eb9-3ef5-b272-14be52e69ed8",
                                                "text": "All this will culminate in a final showdown in Israel between the true Lord (Jehovah) God of Israel and the false god (Allah) of Mecca (the center of pagan idolatry in Arabia, at the Kaaba) […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffcd6773-4773-3478-9f80-ddefd9e213cf",
                                        "entry_id": "c263d298-916a-3a90-b069-45bbe6034df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The first deity of various theistic religions, and the only deity in monotheism.",
                                            "God the Father as distinguished from Jesus Christ, God the Son."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "135d147a-6f38-415d-a6e0-0dd396da96e8",
                                                "sense_id": "ffcd6773-4773-3478-9f80-ddefd9e213cf",
                                                "text": "God sent Jesus to earth to be the King of the Jews; that is, the one to tell them what they should do. […] I will tell you why God let Jesus die upon the cross."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e34578ef-c22d-3e89-a4c4-f50152544383",
                                        "entry_id": "c263d298-916a-3a90-b069-45bbe6034df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The single male deity of various bitheistic or duotheistic religions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd7ae1e9-132c-47db-84c8-4b9f730a870c",
                                                "sense_id": "e34578ef-c22d-3e89-a4c4-f50152544383",
                                                "text": "The ancients represented this fundamental duality mythologically as God and Goddess. When Mystery looks at itself, God looks at Goddess."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bb3d217-5c1a-4f22-b8e5-3522cb6bd34d",
                                                "sense_id": "e34578ef-c22d-3e89-a4c4-f50152544383",
                                                "text": "This reduces the successful invocation of God to a function of the presence of male genitalia. Put another way, women have the wrong equipment to invoke God.\nGoddess and God flow throughout all of nature, through each and every man and woman, becoming fully present in the world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c239cac-718b-4132-9503-83558f55fda9",
                                                "sense_id": "e34578ef-c22d-3e89-a4c4-f50152544383",
                                                "text": "God and Goddess watched as the finite universe continued to develop into a stable platform to sustain finite life and were pleased."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0db51f9a-8ecc-3fcf-b8b7-ca51c239edaa",
                                        "entry_id": "c263d298-916a-3a90-b069-45bbe6034df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The transcendent principle, for example the ultimate cause or prime mover, often not considered as a person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0087b10b-994d-4249-8725-71334ba85ed7",
                                                "sense_id": "0db51f9a-8ecc-3fcf-b8b7-ca51c239edaa",
                                                "text": "God (the great everlasting infinite First Cause from whom all things in heaven and earth proceed) [translating Chinese 道] can neither be defined nor named."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7559aa65-444c-4a34-b4f1-3372434a40fd",
                                                "sense_id": "0db51f9a-8ecc-3fcf-b8b7-ca51c239edaa",
                                                "text": "For Aristotle, God as the ultimate ground is the being that is responsible for the workings of the rational cosmos, but not for itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc496270-836b-4b6d-bfc4-7a09c1bd086b",
                                                "sense_id": "0db51f9a-8ecc-3fcf-b8b7-ca51c239edaa",
                                                "text": "Now, if night, winter, hunger, and war, which describe the God’s appearance as the multiple world, are his ‘scents’ and ‘names’, the same must be true of the world’s several constituents: all created things are just transient ‘scents’, and their names misnomers, of the fiery God."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "God",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f529e452-9e65-30c0-858b-66a8170da34c",
                                        "entry_id": "94544464-8d51-3865-bdb2-ec976300d7a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A being such as a monotheistic God: a single divine creator and ruler of the universe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e598fcc2-a8e7-49d6-a1eb-c049b3fa0146",
                                                "sense_id": "f529e452-9e65-30c0-858b-66a8170da34c",
                                                "text": "A God there is, that guyds the Globe, and framde the fyckle Spheare."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef7cf9e6-67db-4071-a0c4-686f900e8a0d",
                                                "sense_id": "f529e452-9e65-30c0-858b-66a8170da34c",
                                                "text": "The Muéddin: God is great, there is no God but God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4fa1c25-4d74-4149-9789-f6fda8a62395",
                                                "sense_id": "f529e452-9e65-30c0-858b-66a8170da34c",
                                                "text": "Perhaps this... must involve a relationship with a God of truth—and of love, of mercy, of justice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b17a0ed-22af-4441-ac8b-63223a997929",
                                                "sense_id": "f529e452-9e65-30c0-858b-66a8170da34c",
                                                "text": "Whoever said that there isn't a God is full of shit!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "God",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ac6061a-f3c2-3785-8405-89d765bc50ad",
                                        "entry_id": "cb1d211f-1604-3c4c-9442-b9f27c5bb8a0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of oh God: expressing annoyance or frustration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc72de4c-2506-4ef8-8dbf-3ab61db5a1c9",
                                                "sense_id": "9ac6061a-f3c2-3785-8405-89d765bc50ad",
                                                "text": "God, is this because of the \"I don't love you anymore\" T-shirt I bought? It was a joke!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd7c96fc-cbfb-4496-9656-196444e3610a",
                                                "sense_id": "9ac6061a-f3c2-3785-8405-89d765bc50ad",
                                                "text": "Admiral Anderson: God... feels like years since I just sat down."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "221141c0-a87a-41e5-b9c1-9d03352909a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "b595ee63-68d0-3416-a74d-143f89669ad3",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b64c7-8745-3a02-8139-d5d3b1506728",
                        "target_lang_word": "supreme being",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "supreme being",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7717856e-2d28-3640-a9a7-630669a78ad5",
                                        "entry_id": "98af94aa-cda5-38ba-9baf-f90932e9b00a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A god, or a similar deity, characterized by power over all things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b157a8ca-8c16-4583-8d36-294fc7608a68",
                                                "sense_id": "7717856e-2d28-3640-a9a7-630669a78ad5",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: overdeity"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e5c8586-5222-4fc0-8331-f5c541bec6e7",
                                                "sense_id": "7717856e-2d28-3640-a9a7-630669a78ad5",
                                                "text": "And so when they led her from her dungeon, through long, dark corridors, and up a flight of concrete steps to a brilliant courtyard, she went willingly, even gladly—for was she not among the servants of God? It might be, of course, that their interpretation of the supreme being differed from her own, but that they owned a god was sufficient evidence to her that they were kind and good."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
